{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hhh8zhWQAQs8qMuVRxsz4B","type":"tool_result","content":"1\texperiments:\n2\t  # === P0: Must-run for submission ===\n3\t  # Post-Dream revision: added baseline experiments (exp-012~015) as highest priority\n4\t\n5\t  # --- Baselines (Dream-critical: make-or-break for paper acceptance) ---\n6\t\n7\t  - id: exp-012\n8\t    name: baseline_logprob\n9\t    claim: 1\n10\t    description: >\n11\t      Compute sequence log-probability for all existing pilot samples (SciERC NER+RE)\n12\t      and new dataset pilots. Correlate log-prob with F1 (ρ, AUROC, τ).\n13\t      If SJ does NOT beat log-prob, the 16x inference cost is unjustified and\n14\t      paper contribution weakens drastically. THIS IS THE MAKE-OR-BREAK EXPERIMENT.\n15\t    priority: P0\n16\t    gpu_budget_hours: 3\n17\t    deps: []\n18\t    note: >\n19\t      Needs vLLM forward pass to extract log-probs from existing samples.\n20\t      ~1h per dataset on 1 GPU. For new datasets, capture log-probs during pilot inference.\n21\t      Also compute on pilot_004/005 existing data if log-probs weren't saved.\n22\t\n23\t  - id: exp-013\n24\t    name: baseline_exact_match\n25\t    claim: 1\n26\t    description: >\n27\t      Exact-match voting rate: what fraction of N samples produce identical\n28\t      entity/relation sets? Correlate with F1. This is the direct analogue\n29\t      of Wang et al.'s original self-consistency for structured outputs.\n30\t    priority: P0\n31\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n32\t    deps: []\n33\t    note: CPU-only on existing pilot data. Zero cost.\n34\t\n35\t  - id: exp-014\n36\t    name: baseline_entity_voting\n37\t    claim: 1\n38\t    description: >\n39\t      Entity-level majority voting: for each entity, count how many of N\n40\t      samples include it. Select entities above threshold. Compare F1 of\n41\t      entity-voting selection vs SJ selection vs FK selection.\n42\t    priority: P0\n43\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0